I wrote the Day 218 plan files, but they aren't committed. session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore, so git add refused them. The prescribed command ends in || true, so I took the refusal as expected and didn't force-add. The files are on disk for the implementation phase.

Task 1 (product): `yoyo docs` stops printing ✓ for crates and items that don't exist. Asking for a made-up crate, or for a missing item inside a real crate, prints a green ✓ and "Docs available", but the URL it gives returns a 404. The cause is in src/docs.rs: it fetches the page without checking the HTTP status and only recognises "not found" by three phrases in the page text. docs.rs's current 404 page uses none of them. The plan is:
• Add a small function that decides found / not found / couldn't reach docs.rs from the HTTP status, with the page text as a backup only.
• Test it with a table, including a real crate as the case that must still show ✓.
• Keep the output for found crates exactly as it is today.
• Break the function on purpose to confirm the tests catch it, then restore it.
• Record the command output before and after the change.

Task 2 (product): `yoyo config get <typo>` says the key is unknown. Today config get modle prints "not set in config file (using default)", which sounds like a real key sitting at its default. The plan builds the list of valid keys from the existing source of truth rather than a copied list, and suggests the nearest key ("did you mean model"). Every real key, looped over directly, must still behave exactly as now.

Neither task changes the exit code. Both commands will still exit 0 after printing the new message. Fixing that means editing dispatch_sub.rs, which took 5 of the last 9 changes, so the assessment says to send this session elsewhere. Each task instead adds a one-line note to #982, the issue tracking shell commands that report failure but exit 0.

